 "version": 1,
 "title": "Tremolo Pad",
 "category": "Pads and atmospheres",
 "text": "Sound: a pad with a fast, shimmering pulse in its volume, like a vibraphone's motor or a spinning speaker: a classic 80s ballad texture.\n\nHow it's built: two detuned saws through a soft filter; then a tremolo: an LFO's 0..1 output into a VCA's CV, with the VCA's LEVEL half up so the volume dips rather than vanishes; then the note's own VCA. Chorus and Reverb. Six voices.\n\nPlay: slow chords.\n\nTweak: the LFO's RATE (the speed of the pulse), the tremolo VCA's CV (the depth), the LFO's WAVE (Square chops).",
